---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
const updated = '2026-10-11';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy: support and inheritance calculators, no data kept" description="Privacy under the GDPR: income, children and estate figures stay in your browser, no cookies, only the host’s server logs and anonymous error monitoring." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Working out maintenance, divorce costs or an inheritance share means typing in very personal figures. This notice under Articles 12 to 14 GDPR explains what {SITE_URL} learns from them: next to nothing.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. No data protection officer is appointed, as Article 37 GDPR does not require one.</p>
    <h2>2. What happens to your inputs</h2>
    <p>Net income, children’s ages, assets at the wedding, pension entitlements, the value of an estate: the calculators process these only inside your browser. <strong>None of it is sent to us or to anyone else.</strong> So that you can share or revisit a result, the calculator writes your inputs into the address bar; that address stays with you and is not stored by us. Sharing such a link shares the figures in it.</p>
    <h2>3. Processing</h2>
    <h3>Host logs</h3><p>On every page request the host processes technically necessary data (IP address, time, requested address, browser string, referrer) to deliver the page and fend off attacks. Legal basis: Article 6(1)(f) GDPR; retention follows GitHub’s rules.</p>
    <h3>No cookies, no browser storage</h3><p>The site sets no cookies and stores no inputs in your browser.</p>
    <h3>Error monitoring with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free</h3><p>When switched on, Microsoft Clarity in cookie-free mode records loading errors, load times, dead clicks and scrolling anonymously, so that we notice broken calculators. Neither <code>_clck</code> and <code>_clsk</code> nor <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code> are set; each page view gets a fresh identifier, and form fields and page content are masked in the browser. Provider: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland. Legal basis: Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Recordings are deleted after 30 days, aggregated figures after 13 months. You can object by blocking clarity.ms or by writing to us.</p>
    <h2>4. Recipients</h2><p>We sell no data and pass none to law firms, debt collectors or ad networks. Only the host GitHub and, for anonymous error monitoring, Microsoft have access as processors (Article 28 GDPR).</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers outside the EU</h2><p>GitHub, Inc. and Microsoft Corporation are based in the United States and certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework; the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses apply as well (<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a>).</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>You have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability (Articles 15 to 22 GDPR). We answer requests to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> within one month. You may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>) or to the data protection authority of the German state where you live.</p>
    <h2>7. No automated decisions</h2><p>A calculation result has no legal effect and is not a decision within Article 22 GDPR. Maintenance, costs and inheritance shares are decided by courts and authorities.</p>
    <p>See also <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a>. Last updated: {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
